{"source":"read_webpage","text":"Mozilla Developer Network — Using the Fetch API (community translation draft)

The Fetch API provides an interface for fetching resources across the network. The fetch() method takes one mandatory argument, the path to the resource, and returns a Promise. Once the Response is retrieved, several methods are available to define the content type and how it is handled.

Basic usage:

async function logMovies() {
  const response = await fetch('https://api.example/movies');
  const movies = await response.json();
  console.log(movies);
}

Note that fetch rejects only on network failure, not HTTP errors. Check response.ok. Mixed content is blocked when the page is served over HTTPS. CORS headers must permit the origin."}

